# Project: FDRreg Sensitivity Analysis (SNP + MAGMA + SmultiXcan)
# File: fdrreg_sensitivity_analysis_rg.R
# Description: Comprehensive sensitivity analysis for FDRreg across three levels:
#              1. SNP-level:
#                 Reuses harmonised and, when applicable, decorrelated z-scores
#                 from the MAGMA input files generated by fdrreg.R.
#              2. MAGMA gene-level:
#                 No decorrelation and no biological annotations.
#              3. SmultiXcan gene-level:
#                 No decorrelation and no biological annotations.
#
#              Only computes fdr.the (theoretical null), with no LASSO and no
#              covariate contribution analysis.
#
#              The SNP list and gene lists are retained from the original
#              analysis to ensure that sensitivity results are directly
#              comparable with the primary results.
#
# Usage:
#   Rscript fdrreg_sensitivity_analysis_rg.R \
#       --target scz2012 \
#       --traits_with adhd2019,alco2018,bd2018,ed2019,mdd2019,ocd2018 \
#       --traits_no asd2019,cannabis,dx.dep,ever.csh,ever.sh,ever.st,inte,life.threat.accident,mddco,neo.o,neuroti2018,no.dep,physical.crime,ptsd2019,sleep.dura,st.dep \
#       --lasso N \
#       --seed 100
#
# Date: 2026/07/05
# Author: Chief Scientist
# Version: 2.0
# Update: Reuses harmonised MAGMA input files produced by fdrreg.R v2.0.

#-----------------------------#
#---- Configuration Setup ----#
#-----------------------------#

